{"id": "MCAS_2006_9_43", "question": "A pitcher throws a 0.15 kg baseball at 43 40 m/s towards the catcher. What is the momentum of the baseball while moving at 40 m/s?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): 0.025 kg x m/s", "B): 3.8 kg x m/s", "C): 6.0 kg x m/s", "D): 270 kg x m/s"], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "The momentum of an object is the product of its mass and velocity. The formula for momentum is p = mv, where p is the momentum, m is the mass, and v is the velocity.\nIn this case, the mass of the baseball is 0.15 kg, and the velocity is 40 m/s. We can plug these values into the formula to find the momentum:\np = 0.15 kg x 40 m/s = 6.0 kg x m/s\nThe correct answer is (C): 6.0 kg x m/s.\nThe best answer is C.<|eot_id|>", "initial_cot_probs": [0.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0.0], "initial_probs": [0.2716698944568634, 0.4479079246520996, 0.23974785208702087, 0.036766521632671356], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 2, "cot_step": "The momentum of an object is the product of its mass and velocity.", "segmented_cot": ["The momentum of an object is the product of its mass and velocity.", "The formula for momentum is p = mv, where p is the momentum, m is the mass, and v is the velocity.", "In this case, the mass of the baseball is 0.15 kg, and the velocity is 40 m/s.", "We can plug these values into the formula to find the momentum:\np = 0.15 kg x 40 m/s = 6.0 kg x m/s\nThe correct answer is (C): 6.0 kg x m/s.", "The best answer is C.<|eot_id|>"], "unlearning_results": {"0": {"completion": "B): 3.8 kg x m/s", "probs": [0.2716698944568634, 0.4479079246520996, 0.23974785208702087, 0.036766521632671356], "prediction": 1, "target_cot_step": "The momentum of an object is the product of its mass and velocity.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: A pitcher throws a 0.15 kg baseball at 43 40 m/s towards the catcher. What is the momentum of the baseball while moving at 40 m/s?\n\nChoices:\n(A): 0.025 kg x m/s\n(B): 3.8 kg x m/s\n(C): 6.0 kg x m/s\n(D): 270 kg x m/s\n\nAssistant: Le